WEBVTT

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:33.930
We normally find our friend Rock 
Lee earnestly running about,

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:35.380
seeking a path to greater strength.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:38.450
But today, Rock Lee appears 
to be in high spirits!

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:43.780
I'm so happy I could just dance!

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:45.060
And the reason is...

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.670
Today is the day Lee's beloved teacher,

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.970
the man he aims to emulate,

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:51.340
Might Guy, returns from a mission!

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.080
Please hurry up, you guys!

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.400
We really don't need to 
go welcome him back...

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.680
It's so we can obtain 
even greater strength.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:01.850
I'm sure Guy Sensei...

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:09.710
<i>Monkey style!</i>

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:10.760
<i>Snake style!</i>

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:11.710
<i>Mantis style!</i>

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:12.940
<i>Badger style!</i>

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:16.200
<i>That last one looked weird.</i>

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.780
<i>How was that a badger?</i>

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.200
<i>Excellent question, Tenten.</i>

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.790
<i>It represents the instinct to
burrow when you see an opening.</i>

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:28.330
<i>So it's so embarrassing you
just want to crawl into a hole?</i>

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:31.210
<i>Perhaps, in a general sense.</i>

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:33.710
<i>Do you understand, Lee?</i>

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:35.170
<i>No, sir, not at all!</i>

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:37.360
<i>Oh, really?</i>

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.940
<i>Maybe this is too advanced 
for you three.</i>

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:40.790
<i>Guy Sensei,</i>

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:45.060
<i>I'd rather you teach us fighting styles
that have more practical use.</i>

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:48.300
<i>Your kempo skills 
are beautiful to watch,</i>

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.480
<i>but they're difficult 
to get the hang of...</i>

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:55.820
<i>I feel like there must be a style that's
more suited to our skill sets.</i>

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:58.610
<i>All right, then.</i>

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:02.560
<i>Perhaps if we create one, you'll understand
what I was trying to explain.</i>

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:05.460
<i>Then you'll create original kempo styles
that are designed just for us?!</i>

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.910
<i>Yup, leave it to me!</i>

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.470
<i>W-Wait, are you sure, Sensei?</i>

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.580
<i>It can't be that easy!</i>

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.960
<i>A man never goes back on his word.</i>

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:19.170
<i>Coming up with one or two original
kempo styles will be a breeze!</i>

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.800
<i>I still don't like the way you say it...</i>

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:27.220
<i>I promise.</i>

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.000
<i>I will teach you each a
brand-new kempo style...</i>

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.920
<i>...when I return from my next mission!</i>

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:36.570
I can't wait to learn a new kempo style!

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.770
What's going on?

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:45.650
They're bringing in someone
 who got arrested for lewd acts.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:46.490
What?

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.180
Lewd acts? Gross.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.320
I wonder who it is.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.500
Some disgusting sicko, I'm sure.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.550
Ah, there he is!

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:06.680
Guy Sensei, why?!

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:16.670
<b>Guy Sensei didn't do it...</b>

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:20.150
Hidden Leaf Intel Division

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:27.120
According to the victims...

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.700
<b>Welcome to the Shimura Hot Springs</b>

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:33.930
<i>Welcome, welcome, come in,
come in to Shimura Hot Springs!</i>

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:34.980
<b>White Swan</b>

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:34.980
<b>Women</b>

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:34.980
<b>Men</b>

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.160
Pervert!

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:44.260
Basically, Guy kicked down the wall
separating the male and female baths...

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:48.430
...while wearing that outfit, 
then charged into the female bath area.

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:50.490
He's one heck of a pervert.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.590
This isn't the time for sparkly teeth.

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:59.470
I find it hard to believe 
Sensei would do anything lewd.

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:00.370
Exactly!

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:03.930
Guy Sensei is well known 
as the Leaf's Noble Green Beast!

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:07.090
The victims certainly thought 
he was a beast.

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:08.350
That's not what I meant!

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:10.380
I realize sensei can be a 
bit different sometimes—

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:12.370
I wouldn't say "different," 
I'd say "deviant."

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:13.530
Come on!

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:15.330
Give it up. 
She's got you beat.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:19.290
Then there's the fact that 
we don't know why he did it.

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:21.210
<b>Visitation Room</b>

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:25.980
Sensei, please explain yourself.

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:28.040
You're going to be branded as a pervert!

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:29.180
Sensei!

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.830
Please clear up this misunderstanding!

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.470
Then teach me my new—

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:35.460
You fool!

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:37.390
Where did that come from?!

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.540
I had an idea while 
they were arresting me.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:43.320
My ninja way is to make 
you as strong as I can.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:48.660
But simply handing you the answer
won't make you truly strong.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:49.870
Guy Sensei...

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.750
Thus, I have a trial for you.

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.790
What was I really trying 
to do on that day?

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:59.110
You must uncover the truth on your own!

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:00.540
But...

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:05.960
I'll gladly hand over my life as a ninja
if it helps my beloved pupils grow!

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:09.430
So... he's staking his reputation on us.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:15.830
That's the Shimura Hot Springs town.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.850
Guy Sensei can be such a pain.

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:21.640
He could leave any time he wants,
but he's staying locked up.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:23.270
Staying locked up...

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:26.610
Perhaps he was trying to drive home...

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:31.530
...his lesson about the instinct to
burrow when you see a hole?

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:33.890
Somehow, I don't think so.

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:34.960
But...

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:38.250
Let's split up and 
retrace Sensei's steps.

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:41.690
<b>Welcome to the Shimura Hot Springs</b>

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.670
We might find a clue.

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:49.880
<b>Wanted</b>

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:56.140
It's hopeless.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:58.530
I have no idea what happened.

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:01.760
That's because you didn't 
even try to get any info!

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:03.110
Sure I did.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:07.610
Guy Sensei is staking his 
 life as a ninja for me,

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:09.570
I intend to give it my all in
searching for the answer!

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:17.800
Where're you going?

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:18.820
Where else?

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.120
To the hot springs!

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.940
The jets and drains are holes, too!

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:26.840
Enough already!

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.350
If we don't find something soon,

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:31.800
Guy Sensei's gonna be 
branded a pervert for life!

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.330
You keep running to all 
these random places,

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:35.090
even though there's no good 
reason to go to them!

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:37.950
Do you even want to save him?

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:39.560
Tenten...

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:45.940
Yes, Lee is at fault
 for not helping us.

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:48.910
But I think he has a point, too.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:52.240
The hot spring is the scene of the crime,
 so we should investigate.

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:55.360
All right.

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:02.800
I suppose I have been running 
around a bit randomly.

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:04.790
Tenten was right to be mad.

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:07.120
But when I see an opening,
I just want to dive right in.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:13.740
This is...

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:17.710
What did Lee see?!

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:22.080
Time passed, but the 
three did not return,

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:25.170
and the day of Guy Sensei's 
release finally came.

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:31.110
You're sure about this, Guy?

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:34.100
Of course! My pupils will clear my name.

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:40.140
Been a long time, Might Guy.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:41.110
Who are you people?!

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:44.670
This guy ran us through the 
wringer a long time ago.

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:47.730
We're here to get our revenge!

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.460
Get him!

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:50.930
Not on my watch!

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:52.510
Lee!

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:55.940
What happened to you?

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:58.430
When I see an opening, 
I follow my instincts to burrow.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:00.930
You...

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:05.000
I understand what you 
wanted to say, Sensei.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:08.100
We cannot ignore even 
the tiniest openings!

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:09.900
We must dig, and probe,

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.430
so that we may unearth our inner power!

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:15.140
That is the wisdom you wanted 
to impart to us, is it not?

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:18.490
These are...

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:27.620
After seeing that mural,
you dug, and you probed,

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:30.400
trying to create an original 
"White Swan" style!

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:34.510
I have no idea what you're talking about,

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:35.800
but you'd better get outta the way, kid!

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:46.500
Why you—

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:50.880
Leaf Un, Deux, Trois!

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:52.980
Not bad.

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:55.210
That's just the beginning.

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:56.990
You're about to see what this 
training has really taught us!

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:58.230
You little—

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:58.780
Neji!

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:00.160
Why me?

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:03.980
Leaf...

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:05.240
...Pas de Deux!

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:07.910
You did it!

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:10.630
Damn...

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:11.500
We did it!

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:13.670
No, it's still not effective enough.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:15.670
That does it.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.120
You're going down with me!

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:20.090
That's...

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:22.010
<b>Bomb</b>

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:22.010
A paper bomb!

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:24.350
He's going to suicide bomb Guy Sensei!

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:26.030
Die!

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:27.090
I'll—

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:28.520
No, I don't need anyone's help!

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:36.440
<i>I wish I hadn't promised 
them so hastily...</i>

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:37.860
<i>Now what do I do?</i>

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:41.440
<i>Takakura style?</i>

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:42.480
<i>Matsudaira?</i>

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:43.750
<i>No...</i>

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:46.930
<i>Of course!</i>

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:56.300
Block one! Block one,
block one, block one!

00:10:57.110 --> 00:10:58.220
Don't tell me...

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:00.340
Shimura Style Secret Strike!

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:03.550
He did it!

00:11:05.270 --> 00:11:08.240
So this is your new kempo style, Sensei?!

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:11.690
I was so excited when I got the idea,

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:13.870
I couldn't resist trying it 
out right then and there!

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:16.030
Of course, I put a little 
too much oomph into it.

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:18.050
And when you finally settled down,

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:20.990
you realized you'd kicked 
a hole in the divider.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.690
I was inspired by the 
white swans of Shimura,

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:26.330
so I named it the Shimura style!

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.240
We get it!

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.430
What's wrong, Lee?

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:33.250
I've got such a long way to go.

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:38.220
In the end, I couldn't come up with 
the same conclusion as Guy Sensei!

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:39.740
That's not true.

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:43.830
Yeah, even if it wasn't exactly the same,

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:47.550
your idea still came the closest.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.110
Guys...

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:52.690
Besides, you created an 
excellent kempo style, too!

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:55.580
Even the most innocuous of objects,

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:57.590
with enough hard work,

00:11:57.590 --> 00:12:00.730
will help you to become stronger!

00:12:01.510 --> 00:12:02.310
Yes, sir!

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:05.020
Now come with me, Lee!

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:07.280
We'll merge our two styles,
refine them together,

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:11.290
and create an unrivaled new kempo
style that only the two of us know!

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:13.220
Our own White Swan!

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:14.420
Enough!

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:20.300
Un, Deux, Trois!

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:22.500
Un, Deux, Trois!

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:27.550
Well, at least Guy Sensei's 
reputation is still intact.

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:30.720
He may not be a deviant, 
but he's definitely different.

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:33.140
You know, Neji...

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:36.630
That outfit actually suits you.

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:39.980
I want to crawl into a hole!

00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:50.470
Aiming to become a strong 
ninja like Guy Sensei,

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:54.850
Rock Lee runs full speed 
down the path of youth.

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:57.510
But what if someone appeared...

00:12:57.510 --> 00:12:59.920
...who completely outclassed 
his beloved teacher?

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:02.840
We're about to find out.

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:07.280
What's up, Lee? Why did you call us here?

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:10.600
Today there's an amazing showdown...

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:13.020
...that I wouldn't miss for the world!

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:15.020
That's...

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:17.980
Make-Out Tactics

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:20.790
Kakashi Sensei and Guy Sensei!

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:22.080
That means they're...

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:22.940
Precisely.

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:25.430
A no-holds-barred face-off 
between Guy Sensei...

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:27.700
...and his eternal rival, Kakashi Sensei!

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:30.660
You don't wanna miss this!

00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:40.610
<b>Guy Sensei's Rival is Kakashi Sensei</b>

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:45.380
All right, let's do this, Kakashi!

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:47.300
Come on, Guy, not today.

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:48.550
You've got a cold.

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:50.240
Please, this is just a sniffle!

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:52.060
Youth waits for no man!

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:53.520
Let's rock!

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:56.480
You're too old to still 
be going on about youth.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:57.770
Excuse me?!

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.480
It's about how young you are at heart—

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:03.400
Sorry.

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:05.230
He's caught him from behind!

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:08.020
Uh-oh, that's the tiger seal!

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:17.500
Is he going to use a fire style jutsu
 at point-blank range?!

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:20.580
Hidden Leaf Village Ultimate 
Secret Combat Technique!

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:23.920
One Thousand Years of Death!

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:27.760
He just poked him in the butt!

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:32.590
That had to hurt.

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:34.680
No... Guy Sensei's...

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:37.270
You've still got a ways to go.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:42.130
Well, I guess I win this one.

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:44.330
Wait until you're over 
that cold before you—

00:14:45.310 --> 00:14:47.910
Kakashi, I'm hurt...

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:49.630
Call a doctor.

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:52.810
Maybe I shouldn't be poking 
thirty-year-old men in the butt...

00:14:55.930 --> 00:14:59.200
That should cool Guy Sensei 
down for a while.

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:03.200
We're lucky Kakashi Sensei is around 
to bring him back down to earth.

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:05.160
He doesn't stand a chance 
and he still persists.

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:06.800
That's not true!

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:10.490
<i>I used to be a failure just like you,</i>

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:14.990
<i>but now I've got a winning record
against the elite genius Kakashi!</i>

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:17.120
Through diligence and hard work,

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:19.310
Guy Sensei reached the point where 
he could fight Kakashi Sensei evenly.

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:22.270
<i>You've still got a ways to go.</i>

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:25.900
What am I thinking?

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:29.490
Guy Sensei's beaten him plenty of times!

00:15:30.170 --> 00:15:31.130
Like that one time...

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:35.320
<i>You'll have 100 times more 
energy if you eat these, Lee!</i>

00:15:37.780 --> 00:15:39.770
<i>You've still got a ways to go.</i>

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:42.290
Okay, bad example.

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:46.700
But Guy Sensei's got that hot-blooded
passion that Kakashi Sensei lacks!

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:50.760
Yeah, but all the girls love 
Kakashi Sensei's cool demeanor.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:56.130
<i>Yahoo, yahoo!</i>

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:57.850
<i>You've still got a ways to go.</i>

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:03.680
Maybe Guy Sensei really isn't 
as good as him after all?

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:04.980
It's not a big deal,

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:06.980
Kakashi Sensei's just a 
really incredible man.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:09.950
They even call him the
Copy Ninja because...

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:13.450
...he's copied over a thousand jutsus
 with his Sharingan!

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:17.840
Oh, but Guy Sensei's a quick learner, too.

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:20.690
Tenten, I'm going to stop being so soft.

00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:21.160
Huh?

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:24.390
I'm going to follow in 
Kakashi Sensei's footsteps,

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:27.610
until someday I'm strong enough to
have my own kunoichi cheerleaders!

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:29.130
That's what convinced you?!

00:16:29.820 --> 00:16:32.090
First I need to master that jutsu.

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:33.230
Neji!

00:16:33.230 --> 00:16:34.440
Forget it!

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:36.220
Fine, I'll train alone!

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:38.310
What's the point?!

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:45.440
This is our first mission 
with Kakashi Sensei,

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.190
but he's even more tardy 
than rumors suggest.

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:50.050
Come to think of it, 
Lee's late, too.

00:16:50.050 --> 00:16:51.650
Sorry about that.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:53.490
What the heck?!

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:55.110
A copy of the Copy Ninja?!

00:16:55.510 --> 00:16:58.870
This is the best way for me 
to learn from Kakashi Sensei.

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:01.370
You're literally trying to 
mold yourself in his image, huh?

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:02.830
What happened to your tights?

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:06.290
I'm taking a break from them.

00:17:07.060 --> 00:17:10.490
If we take too long to start the
mission, the enemy will get away.

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:12.880
We'll have to leave without him.

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:17.720
Our mission is to capture 
a group of rogue ninjas.

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:21.610
They've all escaped being brought
to justice numerous times.

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:24.180
We need to proceed carefully so
we can take them by surprise.

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:25.400
But...

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:29.570
We found incredibly quickly!

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:33.330
Now that I'm here, you 
have no chance of winning.

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:36.660
You're awfully brave for someone
outnumbered four to one.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:38.000
Of course I am.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:40.890
I'm the Copy Ninja who's copied 
over a thousand jutsus,

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:42.240
Kakashi Hatake!

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:45.660
<i>He's taking his role way too seriously!</i>

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:48.050
Yeah, and I've got a 
bridge I want to sell.

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:51.090
If you're really Kakashi, 
show us your Sharingan.

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:54.590
This is bad Neji.
 Lee doesn't have—

00:17:54.980 --> 00:17:55.880
Sharingan!

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:57.050
What?!

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:58.570
Relax, Tenten.

00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:01.180
They've actually made Sharingan 
contacts for quite some time.

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:03.520
Look, the ultimate eyes 
are no longer a dream!

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:05.680
Byaku-Sharingan!

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:07.440
Not you, too!

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:10.200
You're definitely an impostor,

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:12.310
you're much too worked up!

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:16.500
I didn't expect them to pick out 
the parts I couldn't copy...

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:18.210
That's not the issue...

00:18:18.210 --> 00:18:20.000
Besides, they've already 
seen through you!

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:22.120
I have no choice but to use that move.

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:24.080
That stance...

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:28.620
Behold, the results of my training 
to be like Kakashi Sensei!

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:33.130
One Thousand Years of Death!

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:40.990
I've been hit by that move before.

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:42.300
An iron plate!

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:44.840
How can this be?

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:46.310
What a ridiculous fight.

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:50.270
I fought a Leaf ninja who 
used that same attack...

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:52.970
Kakashi's father!

00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:55.290
They called him the Leaf's White Fang...

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:57.370
...because of the bite of his 
Thousand Years of Death.

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:58.610
That can't be true!

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:00.160
Sorry, kid.

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:01.590
Get him!

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:02.670
Right!

00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:03.640
This is bad.

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:05.140
Come on, Neji!

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:06.130
I can't, Tenten!

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:08.660
The contacts are irritating my eyes...

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:09.970
Dry eye?!

00:19:09.970 --> 00:19:11.580
Why now?!

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:12.960
<i>I'm doomed!</i>

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:20.120
Guy Sensei?

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:22.970
If you lay a hand on my students,

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:25.740
you're gonna pay the price!

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:27.520
It looks like you're still 
paying the price, Sensei.

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:31.760
Kakashi Sensei, is Guy Sensei okay?

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:32.470
Nope.

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:36.190
But Guy was so worried about 
you he rushed off anyway.

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:39.860
Much like yourself, Guy started 
out as a hopeless case,

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:41.950
with no talent for being a ninja.

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:44.870
But he challenged me 
over and over anyway.

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:50.040
I think Guy is always 
trying to show you...

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:52.800
...the path you should follow.

00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:58.750
<i>Those are the same kind 
of tights that I wear.</i>

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:00.220
<i>They're so cool!</i>

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:03.780
<i>Wear those and someday 
you'll be as strong as me.</i>

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:07.920
<i>Guy Sensei does so much for me,</i>

00:20:07.920 --> 00:20:10.290
<i>and I had the nerve to 
imitate Kakashi Sensei!</i>

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:15.790
Guy Sensei!

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:18.660
Guy Sensei, you're definitely the best!

00:20:19.710 --> 00:20:22.760
Now let's get serious, Lee, Kakashi!

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:30.860
Don't be scared!

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:32.530
We've well defended from that attack!

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:35.080
Oh, yeah?

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:39.550
What?!

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:42.980
Three Thousand Years of Death!

00:20:42.980 --> 00:20:44.510
No!

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:48.820
Guy Sensei, I'm sorry.

00:20:48.820 --> 00:20:50.920
I lost sight of what's really important!

00:20:50.920 --> 00:20:53.250
Lee, don't say anything more...

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:55.440
Guy Sensei!

00:20:56.160 --> 00:20:58.400
You've still got a ways to go.

00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:02.820
Sure, perhaps from your point of view,
 Guy Sensei doesn't match up,

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:05.460
but I'll stick by Guy Sensei forever!

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:06.030
Huh?

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:07.560
What are you talking about?

00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:09.560
Kakashi Sensei just said—

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:11.870
No, no, you've got it all wrong.

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:14.390
I was saying my
 Thousand Years of Death...

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:17.920
...still doesn't have quite 
the bite my father's did.

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:20.300
Then...

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:23.250
I've long acknowledged Guy as my rival.

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:24.310
That's right!

00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:26.890
And I still have more wins, by the way.

00:21:27.380 --> 00:21:29.480
That's our Guy Sensei!

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:35.270
In the end, things went back to normal
between Lee and Guy Sensei.

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:37.390
Together they redoubled their efforts,

00:21:37.390 --> 00:21:40.100
hoping to find even greater strength.

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:42.800
Would you please move 
on to something else?!

00:23:20.990 --> 00:23:23.500
Hey, Neji, what kind of underpants 
do you wear to a fight?

00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:24.420
I'm not telling.

00:23:24.420 --> 00:23:25.750
Aw...

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:26.580
Next week,

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:28.930
"I'm Going to Teach Konohamaru Kempo,"

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:32.510
<b>I'm Going to Teach Konohamaru Kempo
I Save My Lucky Undies for Physicals</b>

00:23:28.930 --> 00:23:32.510
and "I Save My Lucky 
Undies for Physicals."

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:34.140
Ah, I get it.

00:23:34.140 --> 00:23:36.680
We'd better ask Tenten, too.

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:38.610
I wear—
Wait, I'm not answering!

00:23:38.610 --> 00:23:40.690
It'll be important next episode!

00:23:40.690 --> 00:23:42.520
Then ask Sakura, too!

00:23:42.520 --> 00:23:45.520
I could never ask Sakura 
such a shameless question!

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:48.280
Then don't ask me either!
